      "reason": "T48 closed the document-readyState gap (now \"interactive\") and the Element.nodeName casing gap (HTML elements now report the uppercased tag, so the body snapshot's nodeName matches happy-dom byte for byte). The single remaining difference is the entry shape: mad-dom exports the extra createWindow() convenience while happy-dom's package entry does not, so `typeof entry.createWindow` reads \"function\" on mad-dom and \"undefined\" on happy-dom. Aligning the entry surface (making `new Window()` the documented construction path and retiring or masking the createWindow export) is tracked by the follow-up todo T48E; the scenario keeps recording the difference so the ledger stays honest until then.",
