      "subsystem": "facade",
      "scenario": "dom-form-validation",
      "reason": "T40 implements the first-batch form contract (value/name/disabled/checked/selected, form.elements, submit/reset and event order) but not the advanced constraint-validation machinery, and T48 records it as a known gap: MAD DOM's form.checkValidity()/reportValidity() always return true (no ValidityState, no constraint evaluation, no invalid event), while happy-dom evaluates the required/type constraints and exposes the per-control validation surface (validity / validationMessage / setCustomValidity / willValidate / checkValidity). Implementing the WHATWG constraint validation is tracked by the follow-up todo T48C.",
