      "status": "known-gap",
      "subsystem": "facade",
      "scenario": "dom-custom-elements-upgrade",
      "reason": "The T42 registry (define/get/getName/whenDefined) and the synchronous lifecycle reactions match happy-dom; T48A closed the `new DefinedClass()` gap - define now stashes the document/name mint slot on the class prototype, so `new DefinedClass()` casts a real detached element whose localName reads the registered name. Two deliberate deviations remain, both tracked by T48D: happy-dom's CustomElementRegistry.upgrade() is a documented no-op while MAD DOM performs a genuine spec-style upgrade (firing connectedCallback), and the define-after-connect upgrade is in-place in MAD DOM while happy-dom physically replaces the element.",
